# Conjurer — a Typical enemy of the 1997 game, the deck as the original shipped it.
# tier: 3/12 Typical enemies — 14 life, bribe 60 gold
# enemy: Conjurer (1997 in-game name, s30/assets/text/Advstrings.txt @CREATURENAMES)
# designer: Coyote Tex, MicroProse designer/producer — every enemy deck (precon page, ref. 2)
# variant: Original (base game; the enemy deck files are dated 19 September 1996)
# source: ../shandalar-src/Decks.zip:Decks/0260.dck "Conjurer (Ub, 4th)" [Tier 3 — Manalink 3
#   file dated 2016-02-15; its first 14 maindeck lines are the 1997 deck, the 11 lines (60
#   cards) after them are the modern deck Manalink appended and are NOT shipped; its
#   .vNone/.v<Colour> sections are the 1997 colour-keyed swaps]
# source: ../s30/assets/configs/rogues/conjurer.toml (main_cards, sideboard_cards, level 3)
#   [Tier 3 — equals the 1997 prefix above]
# source: ../mage-go/rogue_dck/conjurer.dck [Tier 3 — equals the 1997 prefix]
# cross-check: https://mtg.wiki/page/Shandalar_Enemy_Decks_(Typical) — "Conjurer" (Original)
#   [Tier-web — maindeck agrees]
# group: 1997 originals
name: Conjurer
22 Island
2 Fellwar Stone
4 Prodigal Sorcerer
4 Pirate Ship
2 Wall of Water
2 Wall of Air
2 Counterspell
2 Steal Artifact
2 Animate Artifact
2 Unsummon
4 Rod of Ruin
2 Aladdin's Ring
4 Apprentice Wizard
3 Jayemdae Tome
3 Giant Tortoise
# The 1997 file's colour-keyed sideboard sections. The AI played the maindeck WITHOUT
# .vNone plus the one section matching the player's deck colour (.vNone by default);
# .vNone is folded into the maindeck above, and SB: holds, per name, the largest
# colour-section count minus the .vNone count — the smallest sideboard from which
# every 1997 configuration can be rebuilt by swapping.
#   .vNone   3 Giant Tortoise
#   .vBlack  1 Mahamoti Djinn, 2 Giant Tortoise
#   .vBlue   2 Giant Tortoise, 1 Island Fish Jasconius
#   .vGreen  3 Giant Tortoise
#   .vRed    1 Blue Elemental Blast, 1 Giant Tortoise, 1 Volcanic Eruption
#   .vWhite  3 Power Sink
SB: 1 Mahamoti Djinn
SB: 1 Island Fish Jasconius
SB: 1 Blue Elemental Blast
SB: 1 Volcanic Eruption
SB: 3 Power Sink
